WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.800
 Hi, my name is Jesse Mostipak  

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.440
  and I'm a Developer 
  Advocate here at RStudio. 

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.520
 And today I want to take you on a quick 
  high-level tour of RStudio Cloud 

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.000
 from the perspective of an educator.  

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.320
 When you're getting ready 
  to teach R with RStudio, 

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.080
 you have two main options.  

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:24.720
 One option is to walk learners 
  through downloading and installing both 

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.760
 R and RStudio on their local machine, 
  after which you then have to walk 

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:29.680
 through the installation  

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.720
 of all the necessary packages, 
  as well as loading the packages. 

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.800
 And if you're using Git, 
  you've got to install git. 

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.240
 And more often than not  

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.560
 this process results 
  in spending a significant amount of time 

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.400
 troubleshooting unique installation issues 
  across a variety of operating systems. 

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.640
 Another option is to use RStudio Cloud. 

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.880
 RStudio Cloud is a lightweight, 
  cloud-based solution that allows you 

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.160
 to teach data science using the RStudio 
  IDE directly from your browser. 

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.040
 With RStudio Cloud 
  Git works out of the box 

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.760
 and you can avoid the majority 
  of the installation issues 

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.760
 you are likely to encounter 
  when you have learners  

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.800
 download to their personal computer.  

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.600
 What's more, you don't need any system 
  administration experience or I.T. 

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.280
 support to get your course 
  set up. Let's take a look. 

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:27.200
 Once you log into RStudio cCoud, 
  you have a variety of tools 

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.520
 available to you. In the menu on the left 
  we can take a look at workspaces. 

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.920
 You'll always have 
  your own personal workspace 

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.960
 and you can create additional workspaces 
  for each of your courses, like this. 

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.120
 To avoid having students each download 

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:53.240
 packages to their computer, we can set up 
  all of the projects within our workspace 

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.360
 using a default set of files and packages 
  by creating a base project. 

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.040
 This means we can install all of 
  the packages used throughout our course, 

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.800
 along with any files we want our learners 
  to have access to by default. 

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.440
 And we can update this base project 
  throughout our course as needed. 

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.840
 Let's check out what's available to us 
  within a workspace. 

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.400
 One of the first things we can do 
  is add members to our workspace 

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:30.520
 and set their default permissions either 
  through invitations or by using a link. 

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.720
 In addition to adding learners, 
  this is a fantastic way to get any 

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.720
 co-teachers and teaching assistants 
  added to your workspace so that 

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.880
 they can assist with adding learners 
  and setting up the workspace. 

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.040
 We can also create a new 
  RStudio Project 

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.640
 with a click of a button, 
  which will take us to an R project 

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.400
 that looks like what we'd see in the 
  desktop version of the RStudio IDE. 

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.120
 From here, we can share the Project 
  with our learners and even convert it 

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:57.560
 into an assignment. 
  When we create an assignment as educators 

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.840
 RStudio Cloud automatically 
  makes a copy for our learners 

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.680
 and flags the project with the assignment 
  tag from our perspective, 

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.040
 while showing learners either  

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.280
 a start or continue button 
  for each assignment in their workspace. 

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.680
 Another feature in RStudio  

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.080
 Cloud is the ability for educators 
  to look at a learner's assignment. 

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:18.600
 This means that we can run 
  a learner's work on RStudio Cloud 

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.000
 and better help them to identify 
  and debug any errors. 

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.080
 While this doesn't cover everything 
  you can do with RStudio Cloud, 

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:32.760
 I do hope it inspires you to check out the 
  possibilities at rstudio.cloud 

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.280
 And if you'd like to learn more,  

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.480
 please join us for an RStudio 
  Cloud webinar at one p.m. 

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.160
 Eastern on August 18th, 2021  

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.720
 right here on our YouTube channel. 

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.040
 We'll be showing you a prerecorded video 
  from one of our resident Cloud experts,

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:47.640
 and as the video plays,  

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.200
 RStudio staff will be available in chat 
  to answer all of your questions. 

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.760
 I can't wait to see you there! 

